Fixes
=====

- Fix virtual methods calling - the method is found, but in base class

Framework stuff
===============

- Add serialization/deserialization classes which will enable quick loading pre-parsed scripts
- Create unit tests for that
- Remove that weird access control class from runtime and add it to parser
- Find and eliminate raw pointer usage
	- ScriptCallable is returning raw pointer - it should return std::shared_ptr instead
	- ScriptVariable is taking raw pointer as default value - it should take std::unique_ptr (?) instead
- Create a mechanism that will resolve unlinked calls - eg. functions or statements that are compiled, but rely on other statements/etc. that are not compiled yet
- The test 'ParseUntilAtBegin' takes too much time - take a look at it

Functionality
=============

for ... else
Syntax would be:
```
	for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++)
	{
	}
	else
	{
		// Something that runs if the loop doesn't run at least once
	}
```

----------------------

while ... else
do ... while ... else
Samething as for for ... else, but for while loops, same syntax

